Students will also learn about current legal issues in Australia, and explore these in critical and comparative perspective. There is no assumed knowledge for this course and no pre-requisites.
This course is open to international exchange and study abroad students only.

Topics covered may include:

common and civil law systems and comparative law methodology;

introduction to Australian law - history and principles;

introduction to Australian legal institutions: parliament and democracy; courts and judicial review; and the executive;

